From: sullivan@blaze.cs.jhu.edu (Gregory Sullivan)
Date: Mon, 17 Oct 94 23:39:27 EDT
Subject: [#94-10-290] Free Inquiry: Prometheus Issue

The Fall 1994 issue of the magazine Free Inquiry is entitled:  In Praise of
Prometheus. It contains an article by Max More which introduces readers,
mostly self-professed humanists, to the idea of Extropianism. In his article
``On Becoming Posthuman'', I think More does an excellent job of describing
his philosophy and proselytizing a group which is probably unfamiliar with
his brand of technology infused transcendence.  The issue also contains a
short article entitled ``What is `Consciousness''' by Adam Carley which is
relevant to the thread on uploading and which some might find valuable.
Other stuff: interview with Crick and short article by Kosko.

This issue is quite a change from the Spring 1994 issue:  Thou Shalt Not
Multiply - Overpopulation and Contraception. That issue lamented population
growth and contained only a token dissenting viewpoint which cited Julian
Simon's work.     Gregory Sullivan



